# Always deploy via Git

This project is linked to GitHub and Vercel.

- **Production URL:** https://multibet-seven.vercel.app
- **Repo:** https://github.com/markbailey92/multibet
- **Branch:** `main` → production

**Default after completing user-requested work:** commit relevant changes and deploy by pushing to `main`. Do this without waiting to be asked.

1. Commit the relevant changes (follow the repo’s git commit protocol)
2. `git push origin main`
3. Do **not** use `vercel --prod` / `npx vercel deploy` for routine publishes — git push triggers the Vercel deployment

**Commit author (required for Vercel):** Do **not** change `git config`. For every commit in this repo, set env vars so the author is valid:

```bash
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="markbailey92" \
GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="markbailey92@users.noreply.github.com" \
GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="markbailey92" \
GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="markbailey92@users.noreply.github.com" \
git commit ...
```

Never use `mark.bailey@mark.bailey-Mac` — Vercel rejects it.

Exceptions: skip commit/push only if the user explicitly says not to deploy, or if there are no meaningful changes.

If the GitHub ↔ Vercel link is broken, fix with `npx vercel git connect` after checking remotes.
